// 1969. Iris is eight: hide and seek while her parents talk in the kitchen.

== cold_open
  [card]
Every life ends the same way.
  [pause 0.4]
What it meant is still open.
  [pause 0.6]
-> hide_1969

// The listen mechanic plays these at their times; a line reaches her only where she is.
// Its spots are the `spot` fact's values; the count and its pace are the mechanic's.
== hide_1969
  [listen] [count 20] [beat 1.35] [then found_1969]
MUM: She was at the piano again today. She found middle C on her own.
  [at 2.5] [heard piano, door]
DAD: Then lock it.
  [at 6.5] [heard door]
MUM: You could still play, Frank.
  [at 9.5] [heard piano, door, landing]
  [carried += play]
DAD: Who'd listen?
  [at 12.5] [heard piano]
  [carried += play]
MUM: You gave up the conservatory for us. You don't get to give her up too.
  [at 16] [heard door]
  [carried += gave]
DAD: I'd do it again.
  [at 21] [heard door, landing]
MUM: She has your hands, you know. Look at them sometime.
  [at 24] [heard landing]
  [carried += hands]

== found_1969
  [card] [picture hide]
{ spot = stairs }
  Margaret finds her in four seconds.
  MARGARET: You always hide there.
{ spot = piano }
  Margaret walks past the piano three times. The third time she stops, and listens, and walks on.
{ spot = door }
  The kitchen door opens. Dad looks down at her for a long time.
  DAD: How long have you been there?
  He doesn't wait for an answer.
{ spot = landing }
  Nobody finds her. She falls asleep on the landing with her cheek on the carpet.
- In the morning the piano is locked.
  [pause 0.5]
-> kitchen_1985
